<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wiwa people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wiwa are an Indigenous people of the south-eastern and eastern slopes of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-nevada-de-santa-marta">Sierra Nevada de Santa Marta</a> in northern Colombia, one of the four peoples regarded as heirs of the Tairona. They speak a Chibchan language, Damana, and share with the Kogi, Arhuaco and Kankuamo a tradition led by mamos. Many Wiwa were displaced by Colombia's armed conflict in the late 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wiwa-people.jpg" alt="Wiwa people" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nortizpe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portaretrato_familiar_al_natural_Wiwa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
